<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 07:32:05 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>From memes to political movement, India's 'Cockroach' party leads youth revolt</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260705-india-cockroach-party-transforms-online-satire-into-youth-revolt-cjp-dipke-protest</link><description>
India's Cockroach Janata Party began life as a series of internet memes and has grown into a real-life movement, bringing together young people angry about unemployment and alleged exam fraud. What began five weeks ago as a satirical response to comments by India's chief justice has become a fast-growing campaign which now has political ambitions, even as observers question whether it can survive without more effective organisation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ffffa734-746c-11f1-aeba-432894e2c7a6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 07:30:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg">AFP - NARINDER NANU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Mbappé strikes to send France into last eight showdown with Morocco at World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260705-mbapp%C3%A9-strikes-to-send-france-into-last-eight-showdown-with-morocco-at-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
After a 1-0 win in Saturday's match against Paraguay, France will take on Morocco for the second consecutive World Cup. In 2022 in Qatar, they met to contest a place in the final. Four years later in the United States, they will play for a place in the semi-finals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7dbf706e-783c-11f1-8f4c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T231115Z-1573580904-UP1EM741SEP5P-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-PRY-FRA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7dbf706e-783c-11f1-8f4c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T231115Z-1573580904-UP1EM741SEP5P-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-PRY-FRA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">facf6b1c-7806-11f1-b51b-1b32b5d47903</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 01:10:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7dbf706e-783c-11f1-8f4c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T231115Z-1573580904-UP1EM741SEP5P-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-PRY-FRA.jpg">IMAGN IMAGES via Reuters - JAMES LANG</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>‘International law is our compass’ in global conflict, UN rights chief tells RFI</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-international-law-is-our-compass-in-global-conflict-united-nations-rights-chief-tells-rfi-volker-turk</link><description>
United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker Türk tells RFI that repression in Iran and drone warfare and sexual violence in Sudan show that civilians are paying the highest price for conflicts around the globe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de2b7550-d5ea-11f0-8d41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25344363322854.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de2b7550-d5ea-11f0-8d41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25344363322854.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61d37d34-7524-11f1-aab6-1bff2aa3277d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 18:57:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de2b7550-d5ea-11f0-8d41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25344363322854.jpg">© Martial Trezzini / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Denmark's Vingegaard takes Tour de France lead with 'perfect start'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260704-vingegaard-takes-tour-de-france-lead-with-perfect-start</link><description>
Jonas Vingegaard took the first leader's yellow jersey of the 113th edition of the Tour de France as his Visma-Lease a Bike outfit won Saturday's opening team time-trial in Barcelona.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0e5e06e-77d3-11f1-825c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ed5980bc98f0f4c0dab659677b4bad4a6bdcabbd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0e5e06e-77d3-11f1-825c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ed5980bc98f0f4c0dab659677b4bad4a6bdcabbd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2a79f28-77d3-11f1-8d55-698ce17b38a2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 18:10:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0e5e06e-77d3-11f1-825c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ed5980bc98f0f4c0dab659677b4bad4a6bdcabbd.jpg">© Jeff PACHOUD / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Ounahi stars as Morocco outclass Canada to advance to last eight at World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260704-ounahi-stars-as-morocco-outclass-canada-to-advance-to-last-eight-at-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Azzedine Ounahi scored twice on Saturday to steer Morocco past Canada 3-0 and into the last eight at the World Cup for the second consecutive tournament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35ff99e-77dc-11f1-9ca1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ounahi.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35ff99e-77dc-11f1-9ca1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ounahi.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ae2fcda-77df-11f1-8aaa-8759d18d154f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 19:48:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35ff99e-77dc-11f1-9ca1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ounahi.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - KEVIN C. COX</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Germany's anti-immigration AfD elects new leaders amid mass protests</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-germany-anti-immigration-far-right-afd-elects-new-leaders-amid-mass-protests</link><description>
Tens of thousands of demonstrators gathered in the eastern German city of Erfurt on Saturday, blocking major roads and disrupting public transport, but failed to stop the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) from opening its annual party congress.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5c321bc0-77ad-11f1-b0f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T050757Z-278577338-RC2T6MAHDG7S-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-POLITICS-AFD-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5c321bc0-77ad-11f1-b0f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T050757Z-278577338-RC2T6MAHDG7S-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-POLITICS-AFD-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10a75b06-77b8-11f1-bce4-e155381550b7</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 15:13:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5c321bc0-77ad-11f1-b0f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T050757Z-278577338-RC2T6MAHDG7S-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-POLITICS-AFD-PROTEST.jpg">REUTERS - Christian Mang</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>The 'other kick-off': NGOs warn of domestic violence spike during World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-the-other-kick-off-ngos-warn-of-domestic-violence-spike-during-world-cup</link><description>
With the World Cup in full swing, several NGOs have launched awareness campaigns to prevent domestic abuse – incidents of which studies have shown increase on match nights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6cdae03c-752e-11f1-bff2-cfc0d8bf5aea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 14:25:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg">AFP - SCOTT HEPPELL</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Renard quits as Tunisia boss following World Cup debacle</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260705-renard-quits-as-tunisia-boss-following-world-cup-debacle-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Hervé Renard announced on Saturday that he was leaving his role as Tunisia coach less than three weeks after taking over the job.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/503b3c1c-7810-11f1-a475-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/renard.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/503b3c1c-7810-11f1-a475-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/renard.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4134c228-77e9-11f1-a48e-13fc3833ac53</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 01:43:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/503b3c1c-7810-11f1-a475-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/renard.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - CHARLOTTE WILSON</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Pope Leo urges US and Europe to do more for migrants on 4th July anniversary</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-pope-leo-urges-us-and-europe-to-do-more-for-migrants-on-4th-july-anniversary</link><description>
Pope Leo has urged his fellow Americans to welcome and protect immigrants as the United States marked the 250th anniversary of its independence on Saturday. During a visit to the Italian island of Lampedusa he also pressed Europe to do more for people fleeing war and poverty.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59600404-77a1-11f1-80a4-05107bf6196b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 12:10:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg">AFP - TIZIANA FABI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'They've inflicted yet another assault,' parents say after judges mock mother</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260704-france-parents-say-another-assault-inflicted-when-justice-system-mocks-victims</link><description>
A mother who filed a complaint alleging the sexual assault of her young son said she was mocked by magistrates at a court in Bobigny, just outside Paris, after judges wrote that she had "overreacted". As Justice Minister Gérald Darmanin calls for an inquiry into the case, RFI spoke to the boy's parents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e283644a-747e-11f1-8cc2-432561169cd3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 12:31:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/68c46318-6054-11f1-b652-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4YF2CQ.jpg">© Loïc Venance / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>United States at 250: Looking beyond the founding fathers to unsung revolutionaries</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-united-states-at-250-looks-beyond-founding-fathers-to-hidden-revolutionaries</link><description>
The American Revolution is often examined through the lives of towering figures such as George Washington and Benjamin Franklin. But as the United States marks 250 years since the Declaration of Independence, RFI uncovers the stories of an enslaved spy, a woman who fought disguised as a man and an Oneida healer, all of whom helped shape the fight. Their stories begin long before 1776, with European colonisation, the dispossession of indigenous people and the labour of enslaved Africans.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">939f62d2-7494-11f1-a1c6-d71d79a3479e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 08:50:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg">© Domaine public</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Insurgents attack multiple towns in northern and central Mali, army says</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260704-insurgents-attack-multiple-towns-in-northern-and-central-mali-army-says</link><description>
Jihadists and their separatist ​Tuareg-led allies have hit northern Mali, where government troops and Russian paramilitary forces are based, with fresh coordinated attacks –  striking several towns and a prison, according to the army, residents and security sources.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7bb9c60-0b29-11f0-a589-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Convoi%20arm%C3%A9e%20malienne%20entre%20Anefis%20et%20Gao%202013%20Rebecca%20Blackwell%20AP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7bb9c60-0b29-11f0-a589-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Convoi%20arm%C3%A9e%20malienne%20entre%20Anefis%20et%20Gao%202013%20Rebecca%20Blackwell%20AP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">047062cc-7788-11f1-9ac3-2d4c243098a4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 09:34:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7bb9c60-0b29-11f0-a589-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Convoi%20arm%C3%A9e%20malienne%20entre%20Anefis%20et%20Gao%202013%20Rebecca%20Blackwell%20AP.jpg">AP - Rebecca Blackwell</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US turns 250 as Trump warns of 'attack' on American identity</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-us-turns-250-as-trump-warns-of-attack-on-american-identity</link><description>
America turns 250 on Saturday – a landmark birthday that coincides with a time of deep national division and a president determined to seize the festive centre stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c187212-776f-11f1-80c8-f59519eefc02</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 06:10:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg">© Mandel NGAN / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>El Nino set to be 'strong' as UN warns of heatwaves and floods</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260703-el-nino-set-to-be-strong-as-un-warns-of-heatwaves-and-floods</link><description>
El Nino is here and will quickly develop into a strong event between July and September, fuelling the likelihood of extreme weather, the United Nations' climate agency warned Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41dc8bea-5e7e-11f1-93ef-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/38191d18f1b854ef1546f59b783b0e6e5c1dfc70.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41dc8bea-5e7e-11f1-93ef-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/38191d18f1b854ef1546f59b783b0e6e5c1dfc70.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4576b644-7694-11f1-b4d9-554940d89b4f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 04:04:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41dc8bea-5e7e-11f1-93ef-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/38191d18f1b854ef1546f59b783b0e6e5c1dfc70.jpg">© MARTIN BERNETTI / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC trials experimental treatment for rare Ebola strain as outbreak worsens</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260703-drc-trials-experimental-treatment-for-rare-ebola-strain-as-outbreak-worsens</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo has launched a clinical trial of experimental Ebola treatments as the outbreak continues to spread in the north-east of the country. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b29ced5c-7661-11f1-9665-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-02T204519Z-2059851712-RC2R5MAKUXM2-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO-SOUTHAFRICA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b29ced5c-7661-11f1-9665-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-02T204519Z-2059851712-RC2R5MAKUXM2-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO-SOUTHAFRICA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12d998d6-76b8-11f1-bc7c-09e15d4a7f4e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 09:51:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b29ced5c-7661-11f1-9665-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-02T204519Z-2059851712-RC2R5MAKUXM2-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO-SOUTHAFRICA.jpg">© Arsene Mpiana / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Severe flooding leaves a trail of death and destruction in West Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260703-severe-flooding-leaves-a-trail-of-death-and-destruction-in-west-africa</link><description>
Severe floods have hit Côte d’Ivoire, Ghana, Benin, Togo and Nigeria this week. At least 13 people have been killed in recent days in Ghana and five in Togo, while 59 have died in Côte d’Ivoire since the rainy season began in mid-May.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc44ef1a-74b8-11f1-93ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181667391510.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc44ef1a-74b8-11f1-93ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181667391510.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41dd15f0-7635-11f1-ac2a-b5417acad19a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 14:44:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc44ef1a-74b8-11f1-93ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181667391510.jpg">© AP/Ghana's National Disaster Management Organisation.</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Egypt beat Australia on penalties to reach last 16 for first time at World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260703-egypt-beat-australia-on-penalties-to-reach-last-16-for-first-time-at-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Egypt beat Australia on penalties on Friday to advance to the last 16 at the World Cup for the first time.
